    {
      "id": "c1",
      "kind": "concept",
      "body": "Sometimes you *want* the addition to happen first. **Parentheses** let you say so: whatever sits inside them gets done before anything else. So 2 + 3 × 4 is 14, but (2 + 3) × 4 is 20 — the parentheses force the 2 + 3, then multiply. Grouping symbols outrank the ×÷-first rule.",
      "figure": "dop-grouping"
    },
